    /// - EffectImplement.json holds your configured effect implementations. It will be regenerated automatically after deletion.
    /// - JapaneseDictionary, EBWebView, and diag are temporary files used by some components. You can delete them; they are generated on demand.
    /// ')
    /// </summary>
    public static string AboutAppData_BasicData => $"This is the internal application data of projectFrameCut.{Environment.NewLine}Modifying these files arbitrarily may lead to unexpected behavior; please treat them with caution.{Environment.NewLine}Among them,{Environment.NewLine}- The Plugins folder contains the plugin binaries and data directories.{Environment.NewLine}- The Plugins.json file is your plugin configuration file. Deleting them is equivalent to disabling the corresponding plugins.{Environment.NewLine}- logging is the log directory. You can clean it, but frequent log cleanup may make it difficult to trace previously occurred issues.{Environment.NewLine}- settings.json, settings_a.json, and settings_b.json are your settings. Please do not modify them, otherwise your configuration may be lost.{Environment.NewLine}- ai_settings_text.json, ai_settings_image.json, and ai_settings_video.json are your configured AI model API settings. Deleting them will cause your configuration to be lost.{Environment.NewLine}- TextTemplates.json contains your configured text templates. It will be regenerated automatically after deletion.{Environment.NewLine}- EffectImplement.json holds your configured effect implementations. It will be regenerated automatically after deletion.{Environment.NewLine}- JapaneseDictionary, EBWebView, and diag are temporary files used by some components. You can delete them; they are generated on demand.";
    
